{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102767-2e-who-were-ancient-atlanteans","id":1102767,"title":"[2E] Who were Ancient Atlanteans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-12T05:16:05-07:00","id":1102767,"title":"[2E] Who were Ancient Atlanteans?","content":"In <b>Mage</b> gameline, we have two kinds of people called \u2018Atlanteans\u2019 \u2013 First are proto-Diamond Orders, that went for Atlantis Myth going more and more popular in Greece, becoming faction from Darshana Cults ( see <i>To the Strongest</i> from <b>Dark Eras</b> 1 book ). Second one are Ancient Atlanteans \u2013 builders of Temples of Time Before, inventors of Orichalcum, Thaumium and other Perfected Materials, creators of Adamas and many of Artifacts. They are described mostly in <b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</b> book. <b>In this topic I want to focus on this <u>second</u> category.</b><br /> <br /> We know that in 2E we have MANY Atlantis sites:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2019MtAw 2E, p. 244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantean temples might not be religious structures but most sorcerers treat them with reverence, and a few pray before them. Nobody knows what the Atlanteans worshiped, but mages base diverse theories upon the symbols in old ruins, or visions gleaned from distant corners of the Temenos. Both of these sources are unreliable, for these visions share a critical characteristic with the ruins themselves: <b>They come from many versions of Atlantis.</b> Some believe that there was never a definitive version of Atlantis beyond its Supernal ideal, so all physical evidence is a shadow cast upon Fallen history. <b>Thus, temples represents Greek, Indian, and other structures, twisted by their true origin during an indescribable epoch.</b> Others say that there have been many versions of Atlantis, rising along various tracks of history but Falling into a single continuum: the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>So who were those first builders that\u2019s buildings seems to go outside of Time and Space, simply by existing? What let them make wonders that modern mages cannot replicate? What are your theories on them?</b><br /> <br /> My solution is simple \u2013 <b>All of Ancient Atlanteans were simply Archmasters.</b> Going outside of Space-Time continuum, they got revelation about those secrets of universe that are encoded as \u2018Atlantis\u2019. In previous eras, simply becoming Archmage could grant you this knowledge \u2013 now passing the Threshold is only beginning and MAYBE Ascended know things like rising the structures as Adamas. In preOrders times, each of this Archmasters would becoming leader of their local society and by passing his knowledge to his apprentices, let those small society becomes next Mu, Lemuria, Hyberborea, Garamantean, Agartha, Nine Lokapalas or Greek\u2019s Atlantis sites ( or any other \u2018mythical civilisation\u2019 ). Off course, Time Before Temples can also come from past or future \u2013 but in the end, they were risen by Archmasters and Masters of old eras that could comprehend their Arcanum secrets ( as Supernal Magic IS slowly leaving the Fallen World ) . In other words \u2013 WE MADE THOSE TEMPLES! WE <i>created</i> those Awakened Kingdoms! ( And PCs <i>can</i>, theoretically, become Second Atlanteans - if they become like superArchmages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T07:54:00-07:00","id":1102807,"title":"","content":"Atlantis never existed. That is the simple answer. Every Ruin, every vision, every dream of Atlantis is flawed and false because they're just echoes of the real one; one which came from a universe with different cosmic principles. The Atlantis-that-was might be akin to the Abyss to us; containing and based upon cosmic principles that are utterly foreign to us. If anything about the legends of Atlantis are true - that they rose to conquer the Heavens and cast out the old gods - then the world-that-was might've been utterly inimical to human existence.<br /> <br /> Trying to speculate about what that is like - even finding it <i>desirable</i> - is fruitless, which is a part of the point. All of the in-setting speculation is merely that; Mages finding odd relics of the Time Before and <i>projecting</i> what they want onto them. Maybe there was an Awakened City, maybe it was fantastical beyond compare, but to a disinterested observer, these Ruins look more like Emanation Realms of a dying cosmic principle; one that warps magic in ways distressingly analogous to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Whatever the Time Before looked like, it's probably distressingly unfriendly to humanity.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, Dave did mention, somewhere, I believe, that Mages in the Time Before might be like mini-Archmasters; lacking Paths and such. Whether that is helpful to you, I dunno.)<br /> <br /> This all said, what you could do is have people dwelling in and around Ruins. Proximi, perhaps, whom some enterprising Mage may declare to be the descendants of the True Atlanteans. I feel like that'd be a fun plot hook. And distressingly close to eugenics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T08:11:23-07:00","id":1102816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102767-2e-who-were-ancient-atlanteans?p=1102807#post1102807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Incidentally, Dave did mention, somewhere, I believe, that Mages in the Time Before might be like mini-Archmasters; lacking Paths and such. Whether that is helpful to you, I dunno.)<br /> <br /> This all said, what you could do is have people dwelling in and around Ruins. Proximi, perhaps, whom some enterprising Mage may declare to be the descendants of the True Atlanteans. I feel like that'd be a fun plot hook. And distressingly close to eugenics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legendary Mage Kingdoms - Mu, Lemuria, Garamantean, Agartha - being 'cities around Temples of Time Before' - have SOOO MUCH sense! And having Proximi in there as 'royal bloodline' is only strengthening this idea! Hyperborea is, by canon, place where ancient (Arch?)Masters tried to build their own empire, but Paradox ( or proto-Seers ) do not let them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T16:43:26-07:00","id":1102947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102767-2e-who-were-ancient-atlanteans?p=1102807#post1102807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to speculate about what that is like - even finding it <i>desirable</i> - is fruitless, which is a part of the point. All of the in-setting speculation is merely that; Mages finding odd relics of the Time Before and <i>projecting</i> what they want onto them. Maybe there was an Awakened City, maybe it was fantastical beyond compare, but to a disinterested observer, these Ruins look more like Emanation Realms of a dying cosmic principle; one that warps magic in ways distressingly analogous to the Abyss.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes me think of a possible theory held by some magicians in-world; the possibility being that the Abyss <i>is </i>that old cosmic principle, not truly destroyed, and mindlessly returning to its old place in reality, but unable to otherwise due to the new principles constructed as its usurper/replacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:16:18-07:00","id":1103160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102767-2e-who-were-ancient-atlanteans?p=1102947#post1102947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me think of a possible theory held by some magicians in-world; the possibility being that the Abyss <i>is </i>that old cosmic principle, not truly destroyed, and mindlessly returning to its old place in reality, but unable to otherwise due to the new principles constructed as its usurper/replacement.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be an idea only Scelesti breathe openly, but it'd be plausible. After all, the Abyss didn't exist before the Fall, it did after. What changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:21:53-07:00","id":1103163,"title":"","content":"There's really no reason the Abyss couldn't have existed pre-Fall. The metaphysics of how it interacts with the Fallen/Supernal may have been all that changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T10:41:55-07:00","id":1103202,"title":"","content":"Given that the Abyss contains the anti-truth symbols, it's plausible that it's the Tellurian's &quot;trash can&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for its existence pre-fall, the Scelesti posit that it was already there in the time before, what changed with the fall is that it allowed the abyss to interpose itself between the supernal and the fallen, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}